  * DWC3 / PHY register blocks only when the GCC status registers say their
  * power domain and clocks are on (an access to a gated block would hang).
+ *
+ * ONCLITE (Redmi 7, SDM632 = msm8953): DWC3 (SuperSpeed-capable core, used
+ * at high speed: micro-USB) at 0x07000000, QSCRATCH at +0xf8800, QUSB2 v1
+ * PHY at 0x00079000, GDSC gdsc_usb30 GCC+0x3f078, clocks GCC+0x3f0xx (live
+ * DT ssusb@7000000 / qusb@79000 / gdsc@183f078; Linux msm-clocks-hwio-8953.h;
+ * LK platform/msm8953 iomap.h). LK runs fastboot on this controller and on
+ * `fastboot boot` only stops it (usb30_udc_stop: DCTL RUN_STOP 0), clocks
+ * and GDSC stay on. A normal boot without fastboot never starts LK's USB:
+ * then the probe reports the block off and stops. Default off on onclite
+ * (sweetusb=1 probe, 2 probe + start).
  */
